{
  "_comment": [
    "PR-review sweep — per-project tables for the Phase 0/1/2 sweeper of",
    "T-pr-review-threads-outlive-their-prs. Copy to <data_dir>/config/pr_review_sweep.json",
    "and edit. Consumed by scripts/pr_review_sweep_phase0.py (Phase 0 read-only sweep) and",
    "scripts/pr_review_sweep_phase1.py (Phase 1 A/B split, added once the ledger's can_close()",
    "lands in a follow-up PR).",
    "",
    "This file carries two tables. Both are declarative repository FACTS (per-project data",
    "the operator provides once, not runtime tuning) and share this file because a single",
    "operator/audit action fills them together for a new project — separating them would",
    "let one arrive without the other and silently degrade the sweep. This co-location is",
    "a design requirement, not a coincidence (msg-2177 R-42(1)).",
    "",
    "----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "Table 1 — projects[].{project, owner, repo}",
    "  Design ref: msg-2162 field ③ (the explicit thread_id → owner/repo mapping",
    "  that S0 needs to resolve a PR from a T-pr-review-* thread).",
    "",
    "  Fields:",
    "    project — chatroom-side project slug (e.g. 'spirrow-mindwire'). This is",
    "              what appears as <slug> in T-pr-review-<slug>-N thread ids.",
    "    owner   — GitHub org/owner login (e.g. 'spirrowgames').",
    "    repo    — GitHub repository name (e.g. 'spirrow-mindwire').",
    "",
    "  The thread prefix ('T-pr-review-<project>-') is DERIVED by the loader from",
    "  the project field using the fixed convention documented in msg-2162; it is",
    "  NOT a separate schema field. Deriving here is safe because the prefix is a",
    "  chatroom-internal naming convention, not a cross-namespace guess.",
    "",
    "  Why owner/repo must be explicit: T-pr-review-<slug>-N LOOKS parseable, but",
    "  <slug> is the chatroom-side project name, not the GitHub owner/repo tuple",
    "  the API needs. In this deployment the chatroom slug and the GitHub repo",
    "  name happen to coincide (both 'spirrow-mindwire') — but coincidence today",
    "  does not entail coincidence tomorrow. A repo rename would silently break",
    "  resolution, so the sweep must not GUESS the GitHub tuple from the thread",
    "  prefix. If a project is missing, the sweep must not fabricate the mapping",
    "  either: S0 returns skip (no verdict) for that thread and the operator is",
    "  expected to add the entry.",
    "",
    "  This is why 'project' and 'repo' can carry the same string yet remain",
    "  distinct fields: they are two identifiers in two different namespaces",
    "  (chatroom slug vs GitHub repo name), not a duplicated write. The operator",
    "  must supply both, once each — not the same value in three places.",
    "",
    "  History note: an earlier draft wrapped owner/repo inside a single-key",
    "  thread_prefix_to_repo dict whose only key was the thread prefix. That",
    "  wrapper was structurally pointless (always exactly one key by design) and",
    "  was removed. The thread_prefix was then dropped as an explicit field and",
    "  moved to loader-side derivation, leaving only the two cross-namespace",
    "  identifiers the sweep genuinely cannot infer.",
    "",
    "----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "Table 2 — projects[].gate_active_since",
    "  Design ref: msg-2174 R-39 (per-project gate-activation date used to split",
    "  B_gate from B_legacy) and msg-2177 R-42(1) (co-located with Table 1 in",
    "  this file). Table 2 has no consumer in Phase 0 — it is consumed by the",
    "  Phase 1-b B_gate/B_legacy split that ships in a later PR. It is included",
    "  here because R-42(1) requires that Tables 1 and 2 be populated together",
    "  in a single operator/audit action; splitting the delivery would create a",
    "  window in which one table exists without the other.",
    "",
    "  A PR whose review-condition-false B was terminated (merged) BEFORE",
    "  gate_active_since is B_legacy, not B_gate: no upstream defect can be",
    "  inferred because the gate did not exist at the time. On or after this",
    "  date, the same shape is B_gate and escalates.",
    "",
    "  Two constraints, both fail-closed:",
    "",
    "    1. justification is REQUIRED and must be substantive — a PR number,",
    "       commit SHA, thread msg-id, or configuration change that establishes",
    "       WHEN the gate first ran against merges in this repo. Placeholders",
    "       ('推定', 'unknown', '') are rejected at load time. If you cannot",
    "       write a justification, OMIT THE gate_active_since KEY ENTIRELY (see",
    "       the spirrow-magickit entry below for the shape) — the sweep will",
    "       treat this project as UNDETERMINED for the B_gate/B_legacy split",
    "       only when a review-condition-false B is actually observed",
    "       (msg-2177 R-41: lazy evaluation).",
    "",
    "    2. The date is an inclusive lower bound: terminal_at >= date → B_gate.",
    "       No clock-skew margin applies here (msg-2174 R-39: the date is",
    "       month-grained; the minute-grained skew that R-21's margin covers",
    "       does not affect this boundary).",
    "",
    "  UNDETERMINED handling — a project observed to have >=1 review-condition-",
    "  false B but with gate_active_since absent — is REPORTED but never fills",
    "  B_gate or B_legacy on its own (msg-2179 R-47: state-only report, no",
    "  thread_id list, no split-attempt counts). The sweeper judgment for A",
    "  (A >= 5 → Phase 2) is UNAFFECTED — it does not reference gate_active_since",
    "  (msg-2177 R-41: the two verdicts are independent).",
    "",
    "----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "Populating this file: the operator is expected to write both tables from",
    "repository history — GitHub org for Table 1, PR/commit/setting-change search",
    "for Table 2. Neither value is derivable from the sweep's own input; that",
    "is the whole reason they live in a config file and not in code.",
    "",
    "Values below are illustrative only; they are NOT the production values for",
    "these projects. Every deployment must edit them. The two entries below",
    "deliberately show BOTH valid shapes of Table 2: spirrow-mindwire carries a",
    "populated gate_active_since (the operator knew the activation date and had",
    "evidence to cite); spirrow-magickit OMITS the key entirely (the operator",
    "did not know the date — the sweep will lazily report UNDETERMINED only if",
    "a review-condition-false B actually surfaces there)."
  ],
  "schema_version": 1,
  "projects": [
    {
      "project": "spirrow-mindwire",
      "owner": "spirrowgames",
      "repo": "spirrow-mindwire",
      "gate_active_since": {
        "date": "2025-01-15",
        "justification": "PR #123 (illustrative): first merge on which pr_gate_ledger recorded a can_close() eligibility check for this repo"
      }
    },
    {
      "project": "spirrow-magickit",
      "owner": "spirrowgames",
      "repo": "spirrow-magickit"
    }
  ]
}
